    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0279" n="249" xml:id="pg249"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501 AA/8–1347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hamilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-08-13T15:00:00+02:00">August 13, 1947—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>386. It was President’s view and other high officials that Finland’s Peace Treaty
                    should first go into effect and then Finland would apply for UN membership
                    (Embtel 372, August 1<anchor n="1" xml:id="d156-f1"/>). Finnish Government
                    consequently decided against applying now.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
